Yes, 14 Mill Wynd is in the **Glenarrow Town Centre conservation area**. It is not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

Under the council's windows guidance, replacing windows in a conservation area needs a planning application unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. So if you want to change the material or the glazing pattern (for example, switching from timber to uPVC, or changing the number or arrangement of panes), you will likely need to apply.

If you'd like to confirm before you start, you can contact the planning desk with your proposal. I can't give a formal opinion on whether your specific scheme needs permission, but I can point you to the relevant guidance or look up an existing application by its reference if you have one.
